{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-07f088d3-54cb-45da-bfab-9742f6d06d1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5f277b4ac3b79ca","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-djmhh0e4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by the AMD Instinct validation campaign. It turns the validated ROCm builds into a productized runtime image and serving runtime definition that ships alongside the existing CUDA builds, so RHOAI can serve the cleared model set on AMD Instinct accelerators under KServe InferenceServices.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and release the vLLM ROCm runtime image in the existing vLLM midstream build and release pipeline, for the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Define/extend the serving runtime definition (ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime) for the ROCm vLLM image, requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources, alongside the existing CUDA variants.\n- Ensure the runtime's release alignment with the platform release train, using the upstream ROCm image cadence findings from the validation campaign.\n- Declare the support scope (supported models, driver prerequisites) for the productized runtime.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A productized vLLM ROCm runtime image is built and released through the platform's build pipeline with a green pipeline run.\n- A serving runtime definition exists that deploys the ROCm vLLM image, and the runtime successfully serves each campaign-cleared model under KServe InferenceServices on AMD GPU nodes (serverless and/or raw deployment mode as supported).\n- The runtime image and definition are included in a platform release, with the supported model list and driver prerequisites stated.\n- The support scope matches the go/no-go list from the validation campaign — no model is declared supported without campaign clearance.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Scope is gated by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: productize only the cleared subset; if no model achieves parity, this epic is dropped and the campaign results feed a follow-up strategy.\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and may affect release-train alignment; misalignment is a timing risk, not a scope change.\n- This runtime is additive alongside the existing CUDA builds — it does not replace an existing capability, so no rollback/feature-flag path is required beyond standard release practices.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39646,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8cd0f36882c8f34","agent_id":"a10cfa25a5e863fb5","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"06b97261-2199-43b8-86ac-aa8ee82ec7f5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:07:31.586Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
