{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-62ed1f9c-34d1-4904-8976-a9bc6504811a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a409c459acdbb1d0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-djmhh0e4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic enables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) for jobs managed by the Training Operator: single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJob runs using ROCm-enabled PyTorch images, admitted through Kueue like their CUDA counterparts. It delivers the training-side enablement of the strategy independently of the serving validation campaign, since training can proceed on currently published upstream ROCm PyTorch images.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Validate and enable PyTorchJob execution on ROCm GPU nodes for single- and multi-GPU job topologies, using ROCm-enabled PyTorch training images.\n- Address any Training Operator changes needed for ROCm jobs (resource requests for `amd.com/gpu`, container/env requirements of the ROCm runtime) identified during enablement.\n- Document/validate the recommended ROCm PyTorch training image usage for PyTorchJob specs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm-enabled PyTorch image runs to completion on AMD GPU nodes and is admitted through Kueue.\n- A multi-GPU (and multi-node, where the topology applies) PyTorchJob using a ROCm-enabled PyTorch image runs to completion on AMD GPU nodes and is admitted through Kueue with gang semantics.\n- Job specs requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources are handled correctly by the Training Operator (scheduling and completion).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. (This epic covers the job-execution half; Kueue quota handling is covered separately.)\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Assumes `amd.com/gpu` resources are exposed on nodes via the AMD GPU Operator / ROCm driver stack; environment bring-up is validated by the serving-side validation campaign and is cluster-infrastructure work outside this epic.\n- Functional validation of training on ROCm requires access to AMD Instinct hardware (same availability risk as the validation campaign).\n- Upstream ROCm PyTorch image cadence is controlled by AMD and the PyTorch community.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40330,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8cd0f36882c8f34","agent_id":"a10cfa25a5e863fb5","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"03a3d130-3d30-4079-8262-55e1a5e2c79f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:07:42.268Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
