{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d5d76cf6-3140-4ffc-a4c7-fae38f040221","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a243efd66b8bc682","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-djmhh0e4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic ensures the Distributed Workloads queueing layer (Kueue) handles `amd.com/gpu` resource quota correctly, so ROCm training and serving workloads are admitted under the platform's quota model just like CUDA workloads. It covers quota configuration/coverage for the AMD resource name in the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue model and any Kueue changes the enablement surfaces.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Validate and enable `amd.com/gpu` quota handling in Kueue: ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors and quota accounting for the AMD GPU resource name.\n- Address any Kueue changes needed for `amd.com/gpu` admission (resource flavor coverage, quota accounting) identified during enablement.\n- Provide the recommended queue/quota configuration for AMD GPU workloads (to be reflected in user documentation).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration admits workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources with correct quota accounting, including all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) admission semantics.\n- Quota for `amd.com/gpu` is enforced: workloads exceeding the configured quota stay pending and are admitted when quota frees up.\n- Kueue metrics (pending/admitted workloads per queue) correctly report AMD GPU workload admission.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. (This epic covers the quota-handling half; PyTorchJob execution is covered separately.)\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Assumes `amd.com/gpu` resources are exposed on nodes via the AMD GPU Operator / ROCm driver stack; environment bring-up is validated by the serving-side validation campaign and is cluster-infrastructure work outside this epic.\n- End-to-end validation (a PyTorchJob admitted with `amd.com/gpu` quota) is an acceptance criterion on the training-side epic; this epic's own deliverable is the quota handling layer.\n- Functional validation on real AMD hardware requires the same hardware access as the validation campaign.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40992,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8cd0f36882c8f34","agent_id":"a10cfa25a5e863fb5","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"71c5895d-71f4-49dc-b2cf-19c721dbf5a4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:07:50.982Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
