ing and training documentation to the new AMD/ROCm topics.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list matching the productized runtime's support scope.\n52\t- Published documentation covers ROCm training job usage and `amd.com/gpu` quota configuration.\n53\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented serving runtime, training support, and quota handling (reviewed by the implementing engineers), with discrepancies resolved.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n58\t\n59\t## Risks and Notes\n60\t\n61\t- Content depends on the outcomes of the validation campaign (validated model list) and the productization, training, and quota work; this epic is scheduled after those complete.\n62\t- Priority derived from the strategy's overall priority (Major) per the docs-authoring exception, not from the HLR's P2 label.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a50c77b23f0e55d","agent_id":"adffe34affbaa2eb0","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"f676f784-7aa5-47dd-a292-5b4c6285668b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:10:32.660Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f7047942fe9f4b3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
