{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b996e35b61a085f7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) for jobs managed by the Training Operator: single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJob runs using ROCm-enabled PyTorch images, admitted through Kueue like their CUDA counterparts. It delivers the training-side enablement of the strategy independently of the serving validation campaign, since training can proceed on currently published upstream ROCm PyTorch images.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Validate and enable PyTorchJob execution on ROCm GPU nodes for single- and multi-GPU job topologies, using ROCm-enabled PyTorch training images.\n38\t- Address any Training Operator changes needed for ROCm jobs (resource requests for `amd.com/gpu`, container/env requirements of the ROCm runtime) identified during enablement.\n39\t- Document/validate the recommended ROCm PyTorch training image usage for PyTorchJob specs.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm-enabled PyTorch image runs to completion on AMD GPU nodes and is admitted through Kueue.\n44\t- A multi-GPU (and multi-node, where the topology applies) PyTorchJob using a ROCm-enabled PyTorch image runs to completion on AMD GPU nodes and is admitted through Kueue with gang semantics.\n45\t- Job specs requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources are handled correctly by the Training Operator (scheduling and completion).\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. (This epic covers the job-execution half; Kueue quota handling is covered separately.)\n50\t\n51\t## Risks and Notes\n52\t\n53\t- Assumes `amd.com/gpu` resources are exposed on nodes via the AMD GPU Operator / ROCm driver stack; environment bring-up is validated by the serving-side validation campaign and is cluster-infrastructure work outside this epic.\n54\t- Functional validation of training on ROCm requires access to AMD Instinct hardware (same availability risk as the validation campaign).\n55\t- Upstream ROCm PyTorch image cadence is controlled by AMD and the PyTorch community.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a13b7f549186121c","agent_id":"a6edeccbbb27ae4d1","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"557a23fa-0f5f-42db-ae47-fc62e856522d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:15:52.503Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b996e35b61a085f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
