{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e9e15f6ba289473","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic ensures the Distributed Workloads queueing layer (Kueue) handles `amd.com/gpu` resource quota correctly, so ROCm training and serving workloads are admitted under the platform's quota model just like CUDA workloads. It covers quota configuration/coverage for the AMD resource name in the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue model and any Kueue changes the enablement surfaces.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Validate and enable `amd.com/gpu` quota handling in Kueue: ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors and quota accounting for the AMD GPU resource name.\n38\t- Address any Kueue changes needed for `amd.com/gpu` admission (resource flavor coverage, quota accounting) identified during enablement.\n39\t- Provide the recommended queue/quota configuration for AMD GPU workloads (to be reflected in user documentation).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration admits workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources with correct quota accounting, including all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) admission semantics.\n44\t- Quota for `amd.com/gpu` is enforced: workloads exceeding the configured quota stay pending and are admitted when quota frees up.\n45\t- Kueue metrics (pending/admitted workloads per queue) correctly report AMD GPU workload admission.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. (This epic covers the quota-handling half; PyTorchJob execution is covered separately.)\n50\t\n51\t## Risks and Notes\n52\t\n53\t- Assumes `amd.com/gpu` resources are exposed on nodes via the AMD GPU Operator / ROCm driver stack; environment bring-up is validated by the serving-side validation campaign and is cluster-infrastructure work outside this epic.\n54\t- End-to-end validation (a PyTorchJob admitted with `amd.com/gpu` quota) is an acceptance criterion on the training-side epic; this epic's own deliverable is the quota handling layer.\n55\t- Functional validation on real AMD hardware requires the same hardware access as the validation campaign.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a13b7f549186121c","agent_id":"a6edeccbbb27ae4d1","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"564266b4-fad6-4d3a-9493-0fca43fe80d4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:15:53.177Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e9e15f6ba289473","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
