{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1949cc97498525f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Document supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and validated model\n4\t  list\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n6\tcomponent: Documentation\n7\tteam: RHOAI Docs\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n16\tai_signals:\n17\t  change_specificity: 0\n18\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n19\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n20\t  existing_foundation: 1\n21\t  open_questions: 0\n22\t  external_dependency: 0\n23\t  human_process_gates: -1\n24\t  repo_access: 1\n25\t  architecture_claims: 0\n26\tinvestigation_signals: null\n27\tai_implementability: Medium\n28\tai_implementability_score: 2\n29\tjira_key: null\n30\tbranch: null\n31\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n32\tgate_failure_impact:\n33\t  action: rewrite\n34\t  fallback_approach: On a campaign no-go, rewrite the documentation to cover the campaign\n35\t    outcome (parity findings and training/quota usage on AMD Instinct) with no validated\n36\t    model list; the validated-model-list topic is dropped and the serving-runtime\n37\t    sections document CUDA-only support.\n38\t---\n39\t# Document supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and validated model list\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tThis epic authors the user-facing documentation for AMD GPU (ROCm) enablement: what AMD hardware is supported, the driver and software prerequisites for serving and training on ROCm, and the list of models validated on the ROCm serving runtime. It documents the as-built state of the serving runtime productization, training support, and quota setup.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- New documentation topics covering:\n48\t  - supported AMD Instinct hardware for RHOAI serving and training,\n49\t  - driver and software prerequisites (ROCm driver/runtime, GPU operator/device plugin, node requirements),\n50\t  - the validated model list for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime, as cleared by the validation campaign,\n51\t  - how to run PyTorch training jobs on ROCm and configure `amd.com/gpu` quota in Kueue.\n52\t- Cross-references from existing serving and training documentation to the new AMD/ROCm topics.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list matching the productized runtime's support scope.\n57\t- Published documentation covers ROCm training job usage and `amd.com/gpu` quota configuration.\n58\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented serving runtime, training support, and quota handling (reviewed by the implementing engineers), with discrepancies resolved.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n63\t\n64\t## Risks and Notes\n65\t\n66\t- Content is gated by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome (`gated_by` on this epic): the validated model list is a direct campaign deliverable, and on a no-go the productized-runtime sections fall away. On a no-go, this epic is rewritten to document the campaign outcome (parity findings, training/quota usage on AMD Instinct) with no validated model list; scheduling still waits for the productization, training, and quota work to complete.\n67\t- Priority derived from the strategy's overall priority (Major) per the docs-authoring exception, not from the HLR's P2 label.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a13b7f549186121c","agent_id":"a6edeccbbb27ae4d1","session_id":"bc9ea267-6fda-4bac-95a7-007b50b2b12c","uuid":"7c161b05-c208-4b77-94f4-dd7f0e776039","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:15:53.785Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1949cc97498525f","permission_de